# aero-site repo ignores
#
# THIS REPO IS PUBLIC. The tracked content is the website under site/, plus
# .github/. Everything below belongs to another repo or is local state.
#
# Layout, since 2026-08-08: the parent directory (Projects/Aero) is a plain
# workspace, not a repo. Its children are peers — aero-site/ (this repo, public),
# aero-wiki/ (private) and vod-bench/. Loose working docs live in the workspace,
# outside this tree, where they cannot be committed here by accident.

# --- The wiki is its own repository (rymanov/aero-wiki, PRIVATE) and is the
#     SSOT for product/eng/store/site/brand.
#
#     It appears here as a SYMLINK to ../aero-wiki, deliberately: site/scripts/
#     check-content-sync.py resolves the wiki as REPO_ROOT/aero-wiki, and CI
#     checks it out to that same shape (actions/checkout with path: aero-wiki).
#     The symlink keeps the local layout identical to the CI layout.
#
#     NOTE THE MISSING TRAILING SLASH. "aero-wiki/" matches directories only,
#     and a symlink is a file to git — with the slash this line silently stops
#     ignoring, and the link becomes committable. Leave it as it is. ---
/aero-wiki

# --- Local scratch / handoff / design / prompt docs, should any land at this
#     repo root. They belong in the workspace above, or in the wiki's raw/.
#     Root-level markdown only — site/**/*.md is unaffected. For a genuinely
#     tracked root doc (a real README.md), use `git add -f`. ---
/*.md

# --- Build caches / editor / OS junk ---
.wrangler/
.obsidian/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Local Claude Code harness state (permissions, launch config, worktrees)
.claude/
